<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rudnik</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rudnik is a mountain in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a>, south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgrade">Belgrade</a>, whose name means 'mine'. Its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> and lead mines, worked from the 13th century with the help of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> miners, were among the richest in medieval Serbia. The mining town at its foot changed hands among regional lords such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nikola-altomanovic">Nikola Altomanović</a> and Prince Lazar, and later between the Serbian Despotate and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>.</p></div>
